      "eyebrow": "The law",
      "heading": "Why the check matters",
      "html": "<p>It is an offence to use a vehicle on a road in a dangerous condition. Operator licence holders must keep vehicles fit and safe.</p><p>The DVSA Guide to Maintaining Roadworthiness asks for a daily check of every vehicle before it goes out. The driver reports defects. The operator makes sure the vehicle is safe and keeps the records.</p><p>The Traffic Commissioner looks at your record. Missed checks, defects driven on and gaps in the records all count against you.</p>"
