      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>Is a daily walkaround check a legal requirement for UK operators?</h3><p>Yes. Operators with a goods vehicle or bus licence must not let vehicles run in a dangerous condition. DVSA guidance asks for a daily walkaround check. Poor records count against you when the Traffic Commissioner reviews the licence.</p><h3>How long must walkaround check records be kept?</h3><p>At least 15 months. Keep them ready for DVSA at the operating centre. Electronic records are fine if they cannot be changed afterwards.</p><h3>What happens if a defect is found during the walkaround check?</h3><p>Report it at once to the operator or transport manager. If it affects brakes, steering, tyres or lights, the vehicle must not be used until it is fixed. The driver records the defect. The operator records the fix and the date.</p><h3>Can walkaround checks be completed electronically?</h3><p>Yes, if the record cannot be changed afterwards and is kept for the full period. A WhatsApp check with a timed PDF record can do this.</p>"
